From bccf245a8025c6d3f92dd3561cb8b679c458e274 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 05:48:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09246/11362] The per-arm budget only reached one of the two
 places that cap tokens

Correcting my own incomplete fix, and two wrong diagnoses that followed from it.

ARM_BUDGET was threaded into run_reason_cell_budget's `budget=` argument but NOT
into the LocalGGUFProposer's `max_tokens=`, which kept the module-level 16384. So
the raise never took effect. Max-decoded stayed pinned near 16.9k across the
re-run, and the arm "tested" a 32768 budget it was never actually given.

TWO DIAGNOSES THIS INVALIDATES, both mine, both stated more confidently than the
evidence supported:

  "the limiter is wall-clock, not tokens" -- backwards. 16,384 tokens at ~36 t/s
  is ~470s, plus overhead is the ~489s the cells clustered at. The wall-clock
  number was a CONSEQUENCE of the token cap, not a separate limit. The induce
  timeout is 600s and the proposer timeout is 1800s; neither was ever reached.

  "Qwen3.8 needs use_chat_template=True, per the exp5725 Qwen3.6 fix" -- already
  set. The arm has passed use_chat_template=True since it was written. I proposed
  a fix for a setting that was not wrong.

WHAT IS ACTUALLY ESTABLISHED, from the 13-second raw probe and nothing else:
Qwen3.8-27B terminates naturally on EOS, emits a well-formed ```python fence with
a real step() function, and is not truncated -- 522 tokens, 13.1s. Whatever is
wrong lives in the harness path, and every specific claim I have made about WHICH
part has been wrong so far.

Four hypotheses, four 40-minute runs, and the one cheap probe that produced a fact
came last. The lesson is the same one this week keeps teaching in other people's
code: when a run cannot finish, capture what it actually emits before theorising
about why.
---
 .../experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py            | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py b/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py
index 68beb4644b..6d7a900a3a 100644
--- a/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py
+++ b/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py
@@ -480,7 +480,12 @@ def main() -> int:
             mtp=False,
             kv_quant=KV_QUANT,
             n_ctx=N_CTX,
-            max_tokens=BUDGET,
+            # ARM_BUDGET, not BUDGET. The per-arm budget added earlier only reached
+            # run_reason_cell_budget's `budget=` argument; the PROPOSER kept the module-level
+            # 16384, so the raise never took effect and max-decoded stayed pinned near 16.9k. Two
+            # places had to change and I changed one -- the measurement then "tested" a budget it
+            # was never given.
+            max_tokens=ARM_BUDGET.get(args.arm, BUDGET),
             timeout=1800,
             use_chat_template=True,
             model_path=arm["gguf"],
